{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>besides the burnt-offering of the new moon</b> — On the first day of the seventh month He mentioned \"besides the burnt-offering of the month and its meal-offering,\" but He did not mention the sin-offering of the month, and on Yom HaKippurim He mentioned \"besides the sin-offering of the Kippurim,\" but He did not mention the burnt-offering of the Kippurim. And the reason is that on Yom HaKippurim it is well known that the burnt-offering that He commanded here is in addition to the burnt-offering that He commanded there, for they were commanded on one day but they are not equal, since there (Leviticus 16:5) Israel was commanded only one ram for a burnt-offering, whereas here He commanded for a burnt-offering a bull, a ram, and seven lambs. If so, it is a clear matter that these are additional offerings upon those mentioned there. But the sin-offering, which is identical here and there — one might have erred regarding it and thought that it is the sin-offering mentioned there, for there are not two sin-offerings on one day. Therefore He mentioned it and specified regarding it \"besides the sin-offering of the Kippurim\" — that that sin-offering is the sin-offering of the Kippurim, meaning the inner sin-offering that is burned, which effects atonement upon the Sanctuary from the impurities of the children of Israel and from their transgressions, regarding all their sins, whereas this is an outer sin-offering like the rest of the sin-offerings that come with the additional offerings. And similarly on the day of the first fruits there was no need to say that what He commanded here is in addition to what is stated regarding it in the portion of the appointed times, since on one day two passages were stated regarding it and they are not equal, and there was no need to mention the sin-offering either, because He specified there \"and you shall present with the bread\" (Leviticus 23:18), which makes it a clear matter that all the offerings mentioned there come on account of the bread and are an obligation tied to it, whereas these are additional upon them. But regarding the new moon of the seventh month, it could have been understood that what is stated \"and on your new moons you shall present\" etc. (Numbers 28:11) would apply to all the rest of the months, but in the seventh month its entire offering would be only this offering that He introduced for it. Therefore it was necessary to say \"besides the burnt-offering of the month and its meal-offering.\" And since He mentioned this, we have already learned that everything that appears in the portion of \"and on your new moons\" is a commandment for all the months, including the sin-offering as well, and there was no need to say \"besides the burnt-offering of the month and its meal-offering and its sin-offering.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The translation follows the Hebrew text as given; the section headings (<b>…</b>) are reconstructed from the lemma at the beginning of the comment."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:31.688633975Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}